// LOCATION 360 — the fan-out "brain", proved with ZERO auth.
//
// From one postcode, Orbital fans out across THREE independent APIs in parallel:
//   Postcodes.io  -> coordinates + administrative geography
//   Police.uk     -> street crime near that point   (needs lat/lng)
//   Environment Agency -> flood stations near that point (needs lat/lng)
//
// Orbital invents the Postcodes.io hop once and reuses its coordinates for both
// downstream calls. No integration between these APIs is declared anywhere.
// (Swap the postcode for a company once the Companies House key is wired — see company-360.taxi.)
given { pc : uk.gov.Postcode = "EC2R 8AH" }
find {
  geography : uk.gov.apis.postcodes_io.PostcodeLookup
  crimesNearHq : uk.gov.apis.police_uk.StreetCrime[]
  floodStationsNearHq : uk.gov.apis.environment_agency_flood.FloodStation[]
}
